    {
      "id": "s1",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "NEWS",
      "headline": "NVIDIA's robot model learns from people",
      "source": "research.nvidia.com · blogs.nvidia.com",
      "sourceDate": "Nov 9, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://research.nvidia.com/labs/gear/gr00t-2/",
        "https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/robotics-simulation-advancements-corl/"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story one. NVIDIA introduced Groot two, a new model for controlling robots.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_hero.png",
            "credit": "research.nvidia.com (NVIDIA)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "NVIDIA calls it a world action model.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "acronym",
            "letters": [
              {
                "letter": "W",
                "word": "World"
              },
              {
                "letter": "A",
                "word": "Action"
              },
              {
                "letter": "M",
                "word": "Model"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "It reads what its cameras just saw, imagines how the scene should change next, and plans its moves at the same time. A bit like picturing a move as you make it.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "👁️",
                "label": "Watches",
                "sub": "the last moment of video",
                "cue": "reads"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🔮",
                "label": "Imagines",
                "sub": "how the scene should change",
                "cue": "imagines"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🤲",
                "label": "Acts",
                "sub": "plans the movement too",
                "cue": "plans"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "One model predicts the future video and the robot's actions together.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_q_arch.png",
            "credit": "research.nvidia.com (NVIDIA)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "It learned from four hundred two thousand, seven hundred thirty hours of video of people at work.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_q_data.png",
            "credit": "research.nvidia.com (NVIDIA)"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "So a skill shown only by people can carry over to a robot that never practiced it.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "split",
            "items": [
              {
                "src": "assets/g_vfilter_3s.png",
                "label": "Shown by a person",
                "cue": "people"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/g_vfilter_12s.png",
                "label": "Done by the robot",
                "cue": "robot"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Video still: NVIDIA"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "NVIDIA tested it on fifty tasks the target robot had never done.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/g_vreel_3s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: NVIDIA",
            "fit": "contain"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "With no practice at all, it succeeded at least once on forty of them.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "to": 40,
                "suffix": " / 50",
                "label": "tasks, zero-shot",
                "cue": "forty"
              }
            ],
            "side": "assets/g_q_zero.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "One demonstration per task lifted success to seventy-one percent. Five demonstrations, under three minutes of robot data, lifted it to ninety-five percent.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "to": 71,
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "with 1 demo",
                "cue": "seventy"
              },
              {
                "to": 95,
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "with 5 demos",
                "cue": "ninety"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Those are NVIDIA's own results, from its research page.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_q_shots.png",
            "credit": "research.nvidia.com (NVIDIA)",
            "stamp": "Self-reported"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "It can also take orders from a reasoning AI agent, which breaks a long job into steps.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/g_vplane_60s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: NVIDIA"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "That way, it built a toy plane, a toy tractor and a Hot Wheels car in ninety-eight, ninety-seven and ninety-seven of one hundred trials.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "to": 98,
                "label": "of 100 · toy plane",
                "cue": "ninety"
              },
              {
                "to": 97,
                "label": "of 100 · toy tractor"
              },
              {
                "to": 97,
                "label": "of 100 · Hot Wheels car"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Again, NVIDIA's own trials.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/g_q_agent.png",
            "credit": "research.nvidia.com (NVIDIA)",
            "stamp": "Self-reported"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "A smaller version, Groot two Turbo, runs on the Unitree G1 humanoid itself.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/g_vpop_20s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: NVIDIA"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters. Because it learned so much from human video, a new task needed only minutes of the robot's own data in these tests.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "🧑‍🔧",
              "title": "Learn from people",
              "sub": "hours of human video",
              "cue": "videos"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "⏱️",
              "title": "Adapt fast",
              "sub": "5 demos, under 3 minutes",
              "cue": "minutes"
            }
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. These are NVIDIA's own tests. The code is listed as available in December, and no date or licence for the model weights is given.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Detailed results and videos",
                "cue": "tests"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "NVIDIA's own tests",
                "cue": "NVIDIA's"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Code: \"Available in December\"",
                "cue": "code"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "Weights: no date or licence given",
                "cue": "weights"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "reality"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "NEWS",
      "headline": "Google's robot brain goes to the factory",
      "source": "deepmind.google · x.com/GoogleDeepMind",
      "sourceDate": "Nov 10, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://deepmind.google/blog/gemini-robotics-2-5-accelerates-real-world-physical-intelligence/",
        "https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2120169796184478162"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story two. Google DeepMind introduced Gemini Robotics two point five.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/s1_hero.png",
            "credit": "deepmind.google"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "DeepMind calls it its most capable V L A so far. Vision, language, action. It sees the scene, understands an everyday instruction, and turns that into movement.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "acronym",
            "letters": [
              {
                "letter": "V",
                "word": "Vision"
              },
              {
                "letter": "L",
                "word": "Language"
              },
              {
                "letter": "A",
                "word": "Action"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "It works with different robots, including Apptronik's Apollo 2 humanoid.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/dm_hero_5s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "DeepMind evaluated it across two hundred distinct tasks.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/d_q_200.png",
            "credit": "deepmind.google"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Compared with its earlier models, success was thirty to one hundred percent higher, depending on the task, and tasks were done twenty to thirty percent faster.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "from": 0,
                "to": 100,
                "prefix": "+30–",
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "higher success rate",
                "cue": "thirty"
              },
              {
                "from": 0,
                "to": 30,
                "prefix": "20–",
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "faster",
                "cue": "twenty"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Those are DeepMind's own numbers, measured against its own previous models.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/s1_quote.png",
            "credit": "deepmind.google",
            "stamp": "Self-reported"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Then came a test on a real factory floor.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Lab → Factory"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "In a proof of concept with Apptronik and Mercedes-Benz,",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/dm_merc_2s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind",
            "pan": "out"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Apollo 2 humanoids worked on active production lines in Hungary and Germany.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/dm_merc_12s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind",
            "tags": [
              "Kecskemét, Hungary",
              "Sindelfingen, Germany"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The job is called kitting. The robot sorts parts from bulk bins into trays, in the exact order each vehicle needs.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kitting"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "In that pilot, it reached a ninety-six percent success rate.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "side": "assets/s2_tweet.png",
            "items": [
              {
                "to": 96,
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "success in the pilot",
                "cue": "ninety"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Google DeepMind on X"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "DeepMind calls that promising progress toward real-world industrial use.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/d_q_96.png",
            "credit": "deepmind.google"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters. Apptronik's CEO, Jeff Cardenas, says the models improved dramatically",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/s1_ceo_quote.png",
            "credit": "deepmind.google"
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "in just a few weeks of post-training, and carried over to Mercedes-Benz production with very little drop-off.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/dm_merc_15s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Google DeepMind",
            "pan": "right"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. This was a proof of concept. DeepMind didn't publish the pilot's size or trial counts.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Real production lines",
                "cue": "proof"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Proof of concept, not a rollout",
                "cue": "concept"
              },
              {
                "status": "no",
                "text": "Pilot size and trial counts not published",
                "cue": "publish"
              }
            ]
          },
          "section": "reality"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "PAPER",
      "headline": "A humanoid trained in 3 hours on 1 GPU",
      "source": "arXiv:2610.28480 · supermimic.github.io · corl.org",
      "sourceDate": "v2 Nov 9, 2026 (v1 Oct 20)",
      "urls": [
        "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28480",
        "https://supermimic.github.io",
        "https://www.corl.org/program/awards"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story three is a research paper from UC Berkeley, called SuperMimic.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/m_vhero_6s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Liao et al., supermimic.github.io",
            "fit": "contain"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "It was first posted in October, and it's an award finalist at this year's Conference on Robot Learning.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_corl.png",
            "credit": "corl.org",
            "stamp": "Finalist"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The goal is one controller that lets a humanoid copy almost any human movement, from walking to flips.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/m_vflip_1s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Liao et al., supermimic.github.io",
            "fit": "contain"
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "The usual approach is trial and error in a physics simulator, run on a lot of computers at once.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "Trial and error × huge compute"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "SuperMimic first learns a fast model of how the robot's body moves, then practices inside that model, which tells it exactly which way to adjust. Like rehearsing in your head, with a coach.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "flow",
            "steps": [
              {
                "icon": "🖥️",
                "label": "Simulate",
                "sub": "collect real physics",
                "cue": "learns"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🧠",
                "label": "World model",
                "sub": "learns how the body moves",
                "cue": "model"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🔁",
                "label": "Practice",
                "sub": "inside the model",
                "cue": "practices"
              },
              {
                "icon": "🎯",
                "label": "Adjust",
                "sub": "exact direction to improve",
                "cue": "adjust"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The result. In three hours on a single GPU, it beat the score of a leading baseline that trained for seven days on one hundred twenty-eight GPUs.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "🏭",
              "title": "Baseline",
              "sub": "7 days on 128 GPUs",
              "cue": "baseline"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "⚡",
              "title": "SuperMimic",
              "sub": "3 hours on 1 GPU",
              "cue": "three"
            }
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "That's the paper's own comparison, against the released version of that baseline, called SONIC.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_q_abs.png",
            "credit": "arXiv:2610.28480"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Out of one hundred twenty-nine thousand, five hundred fourteen motions, it failed on only twenty-five, versus one hundred seventy-nine for the baseline.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "to": 25,
                "label": "failed (SuperMimic)",
                "cue": "only"
              },
              {
                "to": 179,
                "label": "failed (baseline)",
                "cue": "versus"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "After nine point eight hours on two GPUs, it had zero failures.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_q_fail.png",
            "credit": "arXiv:2610.28480"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "And the controller transfers to a real Unitree G1 humanoid, including acrobatic moves.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "photo",
            "src": "assets/m_vreal_6s.png",
            "credit": "Video still: Liao et al., supermimic.github.io"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters. The authors say this removes compute as the bottleneck for humanoid control.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "“Compute is no longer the bottleneck.”",
            "sub": "The authors"
          },
          "section": "matters"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Reality check. The test motions were also training motions.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/m_q_cov.png",
            "credit": "supermimic.github.io"
          },
          "section": "reality"
        },
        {
          "narration": "So, as the authors note, the counts measure coverage, not generalization. And the baseline's figures are as they report them.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "checklist",
            "title": "Reality check",
            "items": [
              {
                "status": "ok",
                "text": "Accepted at CoRL 2026 (oral)"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Listed as an award finalist"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Measures coverage, not generalization",
                "cue": "coverage"
              },
              {
                "status": "warn",
                "text": "Baseline figures as the authors report",
                "cue": "baseline's"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "kind": "story",
      "label": "NEWS",
      "headline": "A general AI model controls robot arms",
      "source": "anthropic.com",
      "sourceDate": "Nov 9, 2026",
      "urls": [
        "https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-2"
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "narration": "Story four. Anthropic announced Claude Fable five point two, with robot-control results.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/c_hero.png",
            "credit": "anthropic.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Fable isn't built specifically for robots. It's a general model, the kind used for coding and reasoning.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "versus",
            "left": {
              "icon": "🦾",
              "title": "Robot-specific AI",
              "sub": "built to control robots",
              "cue": "specifically"
            },
            "right": {
              "icon": "🧠",
              "title": "General model",
              "sub": "coding, reasoning, vision",
              "cue": "general"
            }
          },
          "section": "plain"
        },
        {
          "narration": "Anthropic says it got substantially better at controlling physical robots than earlier Claude models.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/c_q_skill.png",
            "credit": "anthropic.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Its video shows robots controlled by Fable solving a puzzle cube, unscrewing a bottle cap, and drawing a picture of a robot.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "panels",
            "items": [
              {
                "src": "assets/c_v_1.5s.png",
                "label": "Puzzle cube",
                "cue": "puzzle"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/c_v_2.5s.png",
                "label": "Bottle cap",
                "cue": "unscrewing"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/c_v_7s.png",
                "label": "Drawing a robot",
                "cue": "drawing"
              }
            ],
            "credit": "Video still: Anthropic"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "The main number comes from a public benchmark called RoboDojo.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "kinetic",
            "text": "RoboDojo",
            "sub": "a public robot-control benchmark"
          },
          "section": "evidence"
        },
        {
          "narration": "It tests how well an AI can control a simulated two-arm robot from camera images.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/c_q_robo.png",
            "credit": "anthropic.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "At its highest effort setting, Fable scored sixty-four point nine percent, more than double GPT six Astra, at twenty-nine point eight, and the previous Fable, at twenty-seven point six.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "stat",
            "items": [
              {
                "to": 9,
                "prefix": "64.",
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "Fable 5.2",
                "cue": "sixty"
              },
              {
                "to": 8,
                "prefix": "29.",
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "GPT-6 Astra",
                "cue": "Astra"
              },
              {
                "to": 6,
                "prefix": "27.",
                "suffix": "%",
                "label": "Fable 5.1",
                "cue": "previous"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Those scores are on Anthropic's launch page.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/c_q_score.png",
            "credit": "anthropic.com"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "But they're Anthropic's own simulation tests, run internally, not an independent evaluation.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/c_q_internal.png",
            "credit": "anthropic.com",
            "stamp": "Self-reported"
          }
        },
        {
          "narration": "Why it matters. Anthropic argues that many of AI's benefits depend on acting in the physical world.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "shot",
            "src": "assets/c_q_why.png",
